window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["langchain-level-up"]=[{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0001","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"Why do LLM applications need RAG?","a":"<p>LLMs generate text and answer questions but often <strong>lack current and specific knowledge</strong>, which gives inaccurate outputs. RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) connects the LLM to external data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0002","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"What is the arc of the Level Up LLM Applications with LangChain course?","a":"<p>LangChain basics, similarity search/RAG, Streamlit UI, multi-source Q&amp;A agent, MongoDB Atlas Vector Search, NoSQL (MongoDB) interaction, LangServe REST API, then cloud deployment.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0003","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"What are the prerequisites of the LangChain Level Up course?","a":"<p>Python 3.10+ (syntax, control flow), CLI/venv/<code>pip</code>, 1-2 years of web development, VS Code, and an OpenAI account with credits.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0004","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"How do you create and activate a virtual environment and install requirements?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python3 -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate  # macOS/Linux\n# venv\\Scripts\\activate   # Windows\npip install -r requirements.txt</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0005","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"Which pip commands install the packages of the LangChain Level Up course?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install langchain openai python-dotenv colorama\npip install langchain-openai langchain-community\npip install streamlit pymongo chromadb\npip install langserve fastapi uvicorn\npip install faiss-cpu</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0006","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"What does each key package in the Level Up course do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>langchain</code></td><td>Framework for building LLM apps by composing chains</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>langchain-openai</code> / <code>openai</code></td><td>OpenAI integration / API client</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>langchain-community</code></td><td>Community integrations (FAISS, Chroma, loaders)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>python-dotenv</code></td><td>Load env vars from <code>.env</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>colorama</code></td><td>Colored terminal output</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>faiss-cpu</code></td><td>Facebook AI Similarity Search (vector search)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0007","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"How do you create the OpenAI API key and store it?","a":"<p>On platform.openai.com go to Project API Keys and create a new secret key. Copy it immediately, because it is shown once. Put it in a <code>.env</code> file at the project root.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>echo &#x27;OPENAI_API_KEY=&lt;your-openai-key&gt;&#x27; &gt; .env</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0008","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"How do you load the OpenAI key from <code>.env</code> in Python?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from dotenv import load_dotenv\nimport os\nload_dotenv()\nopenai_api_key = os.getenv(&quot;OPENAI_API_KEY&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0009","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"Do <code>OpenAI()</code> and <code>ChatOpenAI()</code> need the key passed explicitly?","a":"<p>No. They read <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> from the environment automatically once <code>load_dotenv()</code> has run.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0010","card":"q-langchain-level-up-001-1-overview-prerequisites-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s002","q":"How are the exercise repo branches named and how do you switch to one?","a":"<p><code>&lt;chapter&gt;_&lt;video&gt;b</code> is the beginning and <code>&lt;chapter&gt;_&lt;video&gt;e</code> is the end. Switch with <code>git checkout</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>git checkout 05_02b   # Chapter 5, video 2 — beginning\ngit checkout 05_02e   # final version</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0011","card":"q-langchain-level-up-002-2-langchain-basics-model-i-o-prompt-temp","sec":"langchain-level-up-s003","q":"What is the basic flow of a language model in LangChain, and what is a chain?","a":"<p>Every language model takes an <strong>input</strong> and produces an <strong>output</strong>. The flow is format instructions, the LLM generates, then the output is formatted/parsed. A <strong>chain</strong> is a sequence of components (input, model, output).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0012","card":"q-langchain-level-up-003-2-1-first-application-llm-invoke","sec":"langchain-level-up-s004","q":"What are the three steps of the first LangChain application?","a":"<p>Initialize the language model, provide text input and invoke the model, then return the output.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llm = OpenAI()\ndef ask_question(text):\n    # Step 2: Provide text input and invoke the model\n    result = llm.invoke(text)\n    return result</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0013","card":"q-langchain-level-up-003-2-1-first-application-llm-invoke","sec":"langchain-level-up-s004","q":"Which imports does the first LangChain app use?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from dotenv import load_dotenv\nfrom langchain_openai import OpenAI\nfrom colorama import Fore\nload_dotenv()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0014","card":"q-langchain-level-up-003-2-1-first-application-llm-invoke","sec":"langchain-level-up-s004","q":"How does the CLI menu loop of the first app work?","a":"<p>It prints a menu, reads a choice, and for option 1 asks for a question and prints the model's answer. Option 2 prints \"Goodbye!\" and breaks.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def main():\n    while True:\n        print(f&quot;\\n{Fore.CYAN}1. Ask a question&quot;)\n        print(f&quot;2. Exit{Fore.RESET}&quot;)\n        choice = input(&quot;\\nSelect an option: &quot;)\n        if choice == &quot;1&quot;:\n            question = input(f&quot;\\n{Fore.GREEN}Enter your question: {Fore.RESET}&quot;)\n            response = ask_question(question)\n            print(f&quot;\\n{Fore.YELLOW}{response}{Fore.RESET}&quot;)\n        elif choice == &quot;2&quot;:\n            print(&quot;Goodbye!&quot;)\n            break</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0015","card":"q-langchain-level-up-003-2-1-first-application-llm-invoke","sec":"langchain-level-up-s004","q":"How do you run the app, and is the CLI menu loop reused later?","a":"<p>Run <code>python main.py</code>. The menu loop is reused in later chapters, with different <code>ask_question</code> bodies.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python main.py</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0016","card":"q-langchain-level-up-004-2-2-prompt-templates","sec":"langchain-level-up-s005","q":"What is a prompt and what is a <code>PromptTemplate</code>?","a":"<p>A prompt is the set of instructions or inputs that guides model behavior. A <strong>PromptTemplate</strong> is a reusable recipe with <code>{variable}</code> placeholders. It can hold instructions, few-shot examples, context and the question.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0017","card":"q-langchain-level-up-004-2-2-prompt-templates","sec":"langchain-level-up-s005","q":"How do you create a <code>PromptTemplate</code> with a placeholder and fill it?","a":"<p>Use <code>PromptTemplate.from_template</code> and then <code>format</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain.prompts import PromptTemplate\nprompt = PromptTemplate.from_template(\n    &quot;What is a good name for a company that makes {product}?&quot;\n)\nformatted = prompt.format(product=&quot;colorful socks&quot;)\nprint(formatted)\n# &quot;What is a good name for a company that makes colorful socks?&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0018","card":"q-langchain-level-up-004-2-2-prompt-templates","sec":"langchain-level-up-s005","q":"How do you use a prompt template inside the app before calling the model?","a":"<p>Format the template with the user input, then invoke the LLM with the formatted prompt.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt_template = PromptTemplate.from_template(&quot;Tell me a joke about a {topic}?&quot;)\ndef ask_question(user_input):\n    prompt = prompt_template.format(topic=user_input)\n    print(f&quot;Formatted prompt: {prompt}&quot;)\n    result = llm.invoke(prompt)\n    return result</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0019","card":"q-langchain-level-up-005-2-3-lcel-binding-prompt-model-with","sec":"langchain-level-up-s006","q":"What is LCEL and what does <code>chain.invoke()</code> take?","a":"<p><strong>LCEL (LangChain Expression Language)</strong> pipes components together with <code>|</code>. <code>chain.invoke()</code> takes a dict matching the template variables.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0020","card":"q-langchain-level-up-005-2-3-lcel-binding-prompt-model-with","sec":"langchain-level-up-s006","q":"How do you build a prompt-to-model chain with LCEL and run it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt_template = PromptTemplate.from_template(&quot;Tell me a short joke about {topic}&quot;)\nchain = prompt_template | llm       # prompt → model\nresult = chain.invoke({&quot;topic&quot;: &quot;cats&quot;})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0021","card":"q-langchain-level-up-006-2-4-output-parsers","sec":"langchain-level-up-s007","q":"What does <code>StrOutputParser</code> do, and where should it go in a chain?","a":"<p>It converts the model's output <strong>object</strong> (for example an <code>AIMessage</code> wrapper with metadata) into a plain string. Best practice is to make it the last step of the chain.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0022","card":"q-langchain-level-up-006-2-4-output-parsers","sec":"langchain-level-up-s007","q":"How do you add <code>StrOutputParser</code> to a prompt and model chain?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain_core.output_parsers import StrOutputParser\noutput_parser = StrOutputParser()\nchain = prompt_template | llm | output_parser   # prompt → model → parser\nresult = chain.invoke({&quot;topic&quot;: &quot;cats&quot;})\nprint(result)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0023","card":"q-langchain-level-up-006-2-4-output-parsers","sec":"langchain-level-up-s007","q":"What are the roles of <code>prompt_template</code>, <code>llm</code> and <code>output_parser</code> in a chain?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>prompt_template</code></td><td>Formats instructions with user input variables</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>llm</code></td><td>Generates a response from the formatted prompt</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>output_parser</code></td><td>Turns model output object into a clean string</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0024","card":"q-langchain-level-up-007-3-embeddings-vector-store-faiss-retrieve","sec":"langchain-level-up-s008","q":"What is similarity search and what is it used for?","a":"<p>It retrieves dataset content similar to a query. It is used in information retrieval, image recognition, recommenders and NLP.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0025","card":"q-langchain-level-up-007-3-embeddings-vector-store-faiss-retrieve","sec":"langchain-level-up-s008","q":"What are embeddings and how does a query find matches in a vector store?","a":"<p>Embeddings are vector representations of text that preserve semantic relationships. Text goes through an embedding model to become a vector, which is stored in a vector store. Query vectors are compared with stored vectors (cosine similarity) and the top-k closest are returned.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0026","card":"q-langchain-level-up-007-3-embeddings-vector-store-faiss-retrieve","sec":"langchain-level-up-s008","q":"How do you write the RAG prompt template for a FAISS example?","a":"<p>A <code>ChatPromptTemplate</code> that answers only from the <code>{context}</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate\ntemplate = &quot;&quot;&quot;Answer the question based only on the following context:\n{context}\n\nQuestion: {question}\n&quot;&quot;&quot;\nprompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(template)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0027","card":"q-langchain-level-up-007-3-embeddings-vector-store-faiss-retrieve","sec":"langchain-level-up-s008","q":"How do you create embeddings and a FAISS vector store from documents?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain_openai import OpenAIEmbeddings\nfrom langchain_community.vectorstores import FAISS\nfrom langchain_core.documents import Document\n\nembeddings = OpenAIEmbeddings()\ndocuments = [\n    Document(page_content=&quot;harrison worked at kensho&quot;),\n    Document(page_content=&quot;bears like to eat honey&quot;),\n]\nvector_store = FAISS.from_documents(documents, embeddings)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0028","card":"q-langchain-level-up-007-3-embeddings-vector-store-faiss-retrieve","sec":"langchain-level-up-s008","q":"What does <code>similarity_search</code> return and what does <code>k</code> mean?","a":"<p>A list of <code>Document</code> objects. <code>page_content</code> holds the text and <code>metadata</code> holds source, page and so on. <code>k</code> (top_k) is the number of results.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query = &quot;Where did Harrison work?&quot;\nresults = vector_store.similarity_search(query, k=1)\nprint(results[0].page_content)   # &quot;harrison worked at kensho&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0029","card":"q-langchain-level-up-007-3-embeddings-vector-store-faiss-retrieve","sec":"langchain-level-up-s008","q":"How do you use a vector store as a retriever in an LCEL RAG chain?","a":"<p>Wrap it with <code>as_retriever()</code> and put a dict in front of the prompt. The retriever fills <code>{context}</code> and <code>RunnablePassthrough()</code> forwards the raw question unchanged to <code>{question}</code>. The dict runs in parallel.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retriever = vector_store.as_retriever()\nllm = ChatOpenAI()\nchain = (\n    {&quot;context&quot;: retriever, &quot;question&quot;: RunnablePassthrough()}\n    | prompt\n    | llm\n    | StrOutputParser()\n)\nresult = chain.invoke(&quot;Where did Harrison work?&quot;)   # &quot;Harrison worked at Kensho.&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0030","card":"q-langchain-level-up-007-3-embeddings-vector-store-faiss-retrieve","sec":"langchain-level-up-s008","q":"What do <code>similarity_search()</code>, <code>as_retriever()</code> and <code>RunnablePassthrough()</code> do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Concept</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>similarity_search()</code></td><td>Direct method to find similar documents</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>as_retriever()</code></td><td>Wraps a vector store as a retriever usable in chains</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>RunnablePassthrough()</code></td><td>Passes input through unchanged (the question in RAG chains)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0031","card":"q-langchain-level-up-008-4-1-why-rag-architecture","sec":"langchain-level-up-s009","q":"Which LLM limits does RAG fix?","a":"<p>The <strong>training-data cut-off</strong>, <strong>no specialized domain knowledge</strong> and <strong>no access to your private data</strong>. RAG combines retrieval with generation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0032","card":"q-langchain-level-up-008-4-1-why-rag-architecture","sec":"langchain-level-up-s009","q":"What are the benefits of RAG?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Benefit</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Up-to-date information</td><td>Retrieves context from external data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Improved accuracy</td><td>Answers aligned with the actual data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Domain-specific knowledge</td><td>LLM knows your products, services, policies</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0033","card":"q-langchain-level-up-008-4-1-why-rag-architecture","sec":"langchain-level-up-s009","q":"What are the two components of RAG?","a":"<p><strong>Information retrieval</strong> from an external source, and <strong>augmented generation</strong> (the retrieved context is added to the prompt).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0034","card":"q-langchain-level-up-008-4-1-why-rag-architecture","sec":"langchain-level-up-s009","q":"What are the seven stages of a RAG pipeline?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>1. Document indexing</td><td>Split documents into smaller chunks</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>2. Create embeddings</td><td>Chunks → numeric vectors</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>3. Store in vector store</td><td>Save embeddings for efficient similarity search</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>4. User query</td><td>Triggers search</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>5. Retrieval</td><td>Search the store, retrieve relevant documents</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>6. Context integration</td><td>Combine retrieved docs with the original query</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>7. Augmented generation</td><td>LLM answers using query + retrieved docs</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0035","card":"q-langchain-level-up-008-4-1-why-rag-architecture","sec":"langchain-level-up-s009","q":"What is the Red30 Shoes Q&amp;A chatbot project?","a":"<p>A Q&amp;A chatbot for the fictitious <strong>Red30 Shoes</strong>. The data is a <code>.txt</code> FAQ (opening hours 24/7, return policy, shipping costs, product info). The layout is <code>.env</code>, <code>requirements.txt</code>, <code>main.py</code>, a <code>docs/</code> FAQ file and a README. It needs <code>pip install chromadb</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0036","card":"q-langchain-level-up-009-4-2-load-and-split-documents","sec":"langchain-level-up-s010","q":"How do you load a text file and split it into chunks at sentence boundaries?","a":"<p>Use <code>TextLoader</code> and <code>CharacterTextSplitter</code> with <code>separator=\".\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>raw_text = TextLoader(&quot;docs/red30_faq.txt&quot;).load()\ntext_splitter = CharacterTextSplitter(\n    chunk_size=100,       # max characters per chunk\n    chunk_overlap=0,      # no overlap between chunks\n    separator=&quot;.&quot;         # split at sentence boundaries\n)\nchunks = text_splitter.split_documents(raw_text)\nprint(f&quot;Number of chunks: {len(chunks)}&quot;)\nprint(chunks[0].page_content)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0037","card":"q-langchain-level-up-009-4-2-load-and-split-documents","sec":"langchain-level-up-s010","q":"What do <code>chunk_size</code>, <code>chunk_overlap</code> and <code>separator</code> mean in <code>CharacterTextSplitter</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>chunk_size</code></td><td>Max characters per chunk</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>chunk_overlap</code></td><td>Characters shared between adjacent chunks (e.g., 20 keeps context but adds redundancy)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>separator</code></td><td>Split character: <code>\".\"</code> sentences, <code>\"\\n\"</code> lines</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0038","card":"q-langchain-level-up-009-4-2-load-and-split-documents","sec":"langchain-level-up-s010","q":"In the LangChain RAG preview snippet that uses FAISS, which chunk settings are used?","a":"<p><code>chunk_size=500</code> and <code>chunk_overlap=50</code>, with the same flow: load, split, <code>FAISS.from_documents</code>, <code>as_retriever</code>, chain. It is the same pipeline as the Chroma version.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0039","card":"q-langchain-level-up-010-4-3-embeddings-and-chroma-vector-store","sec":"langchain-level-up-s011","q":"What are embeddings in terms of distance and relatedness?","a":"<p>Embeddings are lists of floats. A <strong>small distance means high relatedness</strong>, a large distance means low relatedness.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0040","card":"q-langchain-level-up-010-4-3-embeddings-and-chroma-vector-store","sec":"langchain-level-up-s011","q":"How do you store chunks in Chroma and search them?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain_openai import OpenAIEmbeddings\nfrom langchain_community.vectorstores import Chroma\n\nembeddings = OpenAIEmbeddings()\ndb = Chroma.from_documents(chunks, embeddings)\n\nuser_query = &quot;What is the return policy?&quot;\ndocs = db.similarity_search(user_query)\nfor doc in docs:\n    print(doc.page_content)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0041","card":"q-langchain-level-up-010-4-3-embeddings-and-chroma-vector-store","sec":"langchain-level-up-s011","q":"How do you get the raw embedding of a text with the OpenAI library, and how big is it?","a":"<p>Call <code>openai.embeddings.create</code> and read <code>response.data[0].embedding</code>. For <code>text-embedding-ada-002</code> it has 1536 dimensions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def get_embedding(text, model=&quot;text-embedding-ada-002&quot;):\n    response = openai.embeddings.create(input=text, model=model)\n    return response.data[0].embedding\n\nquery_embedding = get_embedding(user_query)\nprint(f&quot;Query embedding length: {len(query_embedding)}&quot;)\nprint(f&quot;First 5 values: {query_embedding[:5]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0042","card":"q-langchain-level-up-010-4-3-embeddings-and-chroma-vector-store","sec":"langchain-level-up-s011","q":"FAISS vs Chroma?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>FAISS</th><th>Chroma</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Provider</td><td>Facebook/Meta</td><td>Open-source, AI-native</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Storage</td><td>In-memory (default)</td><td>Persistent by default</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Fast similarity search</td><td>Easy setup, persistence</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Install</td><td><code>pip install faiss-cpu</code></td><td><code>pip install chromadb</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0043","card":"q-langchain-level-up-011-4-4-chain-without-vs-with-context","sec":"langchain-level-up-s012","q":"How do you build a chat prompt chain without context for a customer support bot?","a":"<p>Combine a system message and a human message <code>{user_query}</code> into a <code>ChatPromptTemplate</code>, then pipe it into the model and the parser.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>template = &quot;&quot;&quot;You are a customer support specialist who can answer questions \nand assist users with general inquiries.&quot;&quot;&quot;\nsystem_message_prompt_template = SystemMessagePromptTemplate.from_template(template)\nhuman_message_prompt_template = HumanMessagePromptTemplate.from_template(&quot;{user_query}&quot;)\nchat_prompt_template = ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages([\n    system_message_prompt_template,\n    human_message_prompt_template\n])\nmodel = ChatOpenAI()\noutput_parser = StrOutputParser()\nchain = chat_prompt_template | model | output_parser\nresponse = chain.invoke({&quot;user_query&quot;: &quot;What are the shipping costs?&quot;})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0044","card":"q-langchain-level-up-011-4-4-chain-without-vs-with-context","sec":"langchain-level-up-s012","q":"What kind of answer does the chain without context give for \"What are the shipping costs?\"","a":"<p>A generic one (\"Please provide me with the following details...\"), with no Red30 knowledge.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0045","card":"q-langchain-level-up-011-4-4-chain-without-vs-with-context","sec":"langchain-level-up-s012","q":"How do you add context to the customer support chain?","a":"<p>Add <code>{context}</code> to the system message and wire the retriever in with <code>RunnablePassthrough</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>template = &quot;&quot;&quot;You are a customer support specialist who can answer questions \nand assist users with general inquiries based on the following context:\n{context}\n&quot;&quot;&quot;\nhuman_message_prompt_template = HumanMessagePromptTemplate(\n    input_variables=[&quot;question&quot;, &quot;context&quot;],\n    template=&quot;{question}&quot;\n)\nretriever = db.as_retriever()\nchain = (\n    {&quot;context&quot;: retriever, &quot;question&quot;: RunnablePassthrough()}\n    | chat_prompt_template\n    | model\n    | output_parser\n)\nresponse = chain.invoke(&quot;What is the return policy?&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0046","card":"q-langchain-level-up-011-4-4-chain-without-vs-with-context","sec":"langchain-level-up-s012","q":"What does <code>RunnablePassthrough</code> do in the RAG chain with context?","a":"<p>It forwards the user query unchanged to <code>{question}</code> while the retriever searches the store and fills <code>{context}</code>. Both reach the prompt, then the LLM, then the parser.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0047","card":"q-langchain-level-up-011-4-4-chain-without-vs-with-context","sec":"langchain-level-up-s012","q":"Chain without context vs with context (RAG)?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Without context</th><th>With context (RAG)</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Response</td><td>Generic, vague</td><td>Specific, accurate</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Knowledge</td><td>LLM training data only</td><td>LLM + your data</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0048","card":"q-langchain-level-up-011-4-4-chain-without-vs-with-context","sec":"langchain-level-up-s012","q":"What answer does the RAG chain give for the return policy?","a":"<p>A specific one, for example \"returns accepted within 30 days of purchase\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0049","card":"q-langchain-level-up-012-4-5-complete-rag-function","sec":"langchain-level-up-s013","q":"How do you write the load-and-split and vector-store helpers of the complete RAG function?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def load_and_split(file_path):\n    raw_text = TextLoader(file_path).load()\n    splitter = CharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=100, chunk_overlap=0, separator=&quot;.&quot;)\n    return splitter.split_documents(raw_text)\n\ndef create_vector_store(chunks):\n    embeddings = OpenAIEmbeddings()\n    db = Chroma.from_documents(chunks, embeddings)\n    return db.as_retriever()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0050","card":"q-langchain-level-up-012-4-5-complete-rag-function","sec":"langchain-level-up-s013","q":"How does <code>generate_response</code> build and run the RAG chain?","a":"<p>It makes a chat prompt with <code>{context}</code> and <code>{question}</code>, builds the chain with the retriever and <code>RunnablePassthrough</code>, and invokes it with the query.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def generate_response(query, retriever):\n    template = &quot;&quot;&quot;You are a customer support specialist who can answer questions \n    and assist users with general inquiries based on the following context:\n    {context}\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;\n    prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(template + &quot;\\nQuestion: {question}&quot;)\n    model = ChatOpenAI()\n    output_parser = StrOutputParser()\n    chain = (\n        {&quot;context&quot;: retriever, &quot;question&quot;: RunnablePassthrough()}\n        | prompt\n        | model\n        | output_parser\n    )\n    return chain.invoke(query)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0051","card":"q-langchain-level-up-012-4-5-complete-rag-function","sec":"langchain-level-up-s013","q":"How do you call the complete RAG pipeline end to end?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>chunks = load_and_split(&quot;docs/red30_faq.txt&quot;)\nretriever = create_vector_store(chunks)\nresponse = generate_response(&quot;What are the shipping costs?&quot;, retriever)\nprint(response)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0052","card":"q-langchain-level-up-012-4-5-complete-rag-function","sec":"langchain-level-up-s013","q":"What are the three phases of the Red30 RAG pipeline?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>Indexing: TextLoader, CharacterTextSplitter, OpenAIEmbeddings, Chroma.</li>\n  <li>Retrieval: query goes to the retriever, relevant chunks fill <code>{context}</code>, and <code>RunnablePassthrough</code> fills <code>{question}</code>.</li>\n  <li>Generation: the enhanced prompt goes to ChatOpenAI and then StrOutputParser.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0053","card":"q-langchain-level-up-012-4-5-complete-rag-function","sec":"langchain-level-up-s013","q":"What answers does the Red30 chatbot give when tested with <code>python main.py</code>?","a":"<p>Answers match the FAQ, for example 30-day returns and international shipping from $15.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0054","card":"q-langchain-level-up-013-4-6-challenge-context-and-history-aware","sec":"langchain-level-up-s014","q":"What does a chatbot that is context- and history-aware need?","a":"<p>RAG plus conversation memory. It has three building blocks: a <strong>history-aware retriever</strong> (rewrites the question into a standalone one using chat history), a <strong>stuff-documents Q&amp;A chain</strong>, and a <strong>retrieval chain</strong> that combines them.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0055","card":"q-langchain-level-up-013-4-6-challenge-context-and-history-aware","sec":"langchain-level-up-s014","q":"How do you prepare the documents, vector store, retriever and LLM for the history-aware chatbot?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>documents = TextLoader(&quot;docs/faq.txt&quot;).load()\ntext_splitter = CharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=100, chunk_overlap=0, separator=&quot;\\n&quot;)\nchunks = text_splitter.split_documents(documents)\nvector_store = Chroma.from_documents(chunks, OpenAIEmbeddings())\nretriever = vector_store.as_retriever()\nllm = ChatOpenAI()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0056","card":"q-langchain-level-up-013-4-6-challenge-context-and-history-aware","sec":"langchain-level-up-s014","q":"How do you create a history-aware retriever?","a":"<p>Write a prompt that tells the model to reformulate the latest question into a standalone one without answering it, with a <code>MessagesPlaceholder(\"chat_history\")</code>, then call <code>create_history_aware_retriever(llm, retriever, prompt)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain.chains.history_aware_retriever import create_history_aware_retriever\nfrom langchain.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate, MessagesPlaceholder\n\ncontextualize_q_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages([\n    (&quot;system&quot;, contextualize_q_system_prompt),\n    MessagesPlaceholder(&quot;chat_history&quot;),\n    (&quot;human&quot;, &quot;{input}&quot;),\n])\nhistory_aware_retriever = create_history_aware_retriever(\n    llm, retriever, contextualize_q_prompt\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0057","card":"q-langchain-level-up-013-4-6-challenge-context-and-history-aware","sec":"langchain-level-up-s014","q":"What does the contextualize system prompt tell the model?","a":"<p>Given a chat history and the latest user question, formulate a standalone question that can be understood without the history. Do NOT answer the question, only reformulate it if needed and otherwise return it as is.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>contextualize_q_system_prompt = &quot;&quot;&quot;Given a chat history and the latest user question \nwhich might reference context in the chat history, formulate a standalone question \nwhich can be understood without the chat history. Do NOT answer the question, \njust reformulate it if needed and otherwise return it as is.&quot;&quot;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0058","card":"q-langchain-level-up-013-4-6-challenge-context-and-history-aware","sec":"langchain-level-up-s014","q":"How do you create the Q&amp;A chain that stuffs retrieved documents into the prompt?","a":"<p>Use <code>create_stuff_documents_chain(llm, qa_prompt)</code> with a prompt that has <code>{context}</code>, the chat history placeholder and <code>{input}</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain.chains.combine_documents import create_stuff_documents_chain\n\nqa_system_prompt = &quot;&quot;&quot;You are an assistant for question-answering tasks. \nUse the following pieces of retrieved context to answer the question. \nIf you don&#x27;t know the answer, just say that you don&#x27;t know.\n{context}&quot;&quot;&quot;\nqa_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages([\n    (&quot;system&quot;, qa_system_prompt),\n    MessagesPlaceholder(&quot;chat_history&quot;),\n    (&quot;human&quot;, &quot;{input}&quot;),\n])\nquestion_answer_chain = create_stuff_documents_chain(llm, qa_prompt)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0059","card":"q-langchain-level-up-013-4-6-challenge-context-and-history-aware","sec":"langchain-level-up-s014","q":"How do you combine the retriever and Q&amp;A chain and keep chat history across calls?","a":"<p>Use <code>create_retrieval_chain</code>, invoke it with <code>input</code> and <code>chat_history</code>, then append a <code>HumanMessage</code> and an <code>AIMessage</code> to the history. The answer is in <code>response[\"answer\"]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain.chains import create_retrieval_chain\nfrom langchain_core.messages import HumanMessage, AIMessage\n\nrag_chain = create_retrieval_chain(history_aware_retriever, question_answer_chain)\nchat_history = []\n\ndef query(user_query):\n    response = rag_chain.invoke({\n        &quot;input&quot;: user_query,\n        &quot;chat_history&quot;: chat_history\n    })\n    chat_history.extend([\n        HumanMessage(content=user_query),\n        AIMessage(content=response[&quot;answer&quot;])\n    ])\n    return response[&quot;answer&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0060","card":"q-langchain-level-up-013-4-6-challenge-context-and-history-aware","sec":"langchain-level-up-s014","q":"How do you check that the chatbot remembers the conversation?","a":"<p>Ask \"What was my last question?\". It is answered from <code>chat_history</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(query(&quot;What are the opening hours?&quot;))\nprint(query(&quot;What are the shipping costs?&quot;))\nprint(query(&quot;What was my last question?&quot;))   # answered from chat_history</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0061","card":"q-langchain-level-up-013-4-6-challenge-context-and-history-aware","sec":"langchain-level-up-s014","q":"What do <code>create_history_aware_retriever</code>, <code>create_stuff_documents_chain</code>, <code>create_retrieval_chain</code>, <code>MessagesPlaceholder(\"chat_history\")</code> and <code>HumanMessage</code> / <code>AIMessage</code> do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>create_history_aware_retriever</code></td><td>Reformulates the question using chat history before retrieval</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>create_stuff_documents_chain</code></td><td>\"Stuffs\" retrieved docs into the prompt</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>create_retrieval_chain</code></td><td>Combines retriever + Q&amp;A chain; response dict has <code>answer</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>MessagesPlaceholder(\"chat_history\")</code></td><td>Prompt slot for conversation history</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>HumanMessage</code> / <code>AIMessage</code></td><td>Message objects used to track history</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0062","card":"q-langchain-level-up-013-4-6-challenge-context-and-history-aware","sec":"langchain-level-up-s014","q":"Which loader do you use instead of <code>TextLoader</code> for web data?","a":"<p><code>WebBaseLoader</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0063","card":"q-langchain-level-up-014-5-interactive-web-app-with-streamlit","sec":"langchain-level-up-s015","q":"What is Streamlit and why does it suit GenAI prototypes?","a":"<p>An open-source Python library for quickly building interactive web apps. It has a simple API, built-in chat components, live reruns and easy deploy/share.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0064","card":"q-langchain-level-up-014-5-interactive-web-app-with-streamlit","sec":"langchain-level-up-s015","q":"How do you install and run a Streamlit app and where does it open?","a":"<p>Install with pip and run with <code>streamlit run app.py</code>. It opens <code>http://localhost:8501</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install streamlit\nstreamlit run app.py     # opens http://localhost:8501</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0065","card":"q-langchain-level-up-014-5-interactive-web-app-with-streamlit","sec":"langchain-level-up-s015","q":"Which basic Streamlit calls show a title, a header, text and markdown?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import streamlit as st\nst.title(&quot;Q&amp;A App&quot;)           # Page title\nst.header(&quot;Welcome&quot;)          # Header\nst.write(&quot;Hello, world!&quot;)     # Write text\nst.markdown(&quot;**Bold text**&quot;)  # Markdown support</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0066","card":"q-langchain-level-up-014-5-interactive-web-app-with-streamlit","sec":"langchain-level-up-s015","q":"Where does the Streamlit chat app keep chat history, and what about the system message?","a":"<p>In <code>st.session_state</code>, which persists across reruns. The system message is stored but not displayed.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if &quot;messages&quot; not in st.session_state:\n    st.session_state.messages = []\n    st.session_state.messages.append({\n        &quot;role&quot;: &quot;system&quot;,\n        &quot;content&quot;: &quot;You are a helpful assistant. Ask me anything.&quot;\n    })</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0067","card":"q-langchain-level-up-014-5-interactive-web-app-with-streamlit","sec":"langchain-level-up-s015","q":"How does the complete <code>app.py</code> display earlier messages without the system message?","a":"<p>It loops over <code>st.session_state.messages</code> inside a container and skips the <code>system</code> role.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>chat_placeholder = st.container()\nwith chat_placeholder:\n    for message in st.session_state.messages:\n        if message[&quot;role&quot;] != &quot;system&quot;:\n            with st.chat_message(message[&quot;role&quot;]):\n                st.markdown(message[&quot;content&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0068","card":"q-langchain-level-up-014-5-interactive-web-app-with-streamlit","sec":"langchain-level-up-s015","q":"How does the Streamlit app accept input and answer with the RAG function?","a":"<p><code>st.chat_input</code> returns the text. The app stores and shows the user message, calls <code>query(prompt)</code> (the RAG logic from <code>query.py</code>), shows the answer, and stores it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from query import query  # the RAG query function\n\nprompt = st.chat_input(&quot;What&#x27;s up?&quot;)\nif prompt:\n    st.session_state.messages.append({&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: prompt})\n    with st.chat_message(&quot;user&quot;):\n        st.markdown(prompt)\n    response = query(prompt)          # RAG logic\n    with st.chat_message(&quot;assistant&quot;):\n        st.markdown(response)\n    st.session_state.messages.append({&quot;role&quot;: &quot;assistant&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: response})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0069","card":"q-langchain-level-up-014-5-interactive-web-app-with-streamlit","sec":"langchain-level-up-s015","q":"Is the Streamlit bot context-aware and history-aware?","a":"<p>Yes. It is context-aware (RAG over the FAQ) and history-aware (it answers \"What was my first question?\").</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0070","card":"q-langchain-level-up-014-5-interactive-web-app-with-streamlit","sec":"langchain-level-up-s015","q":"What do <code>st.container()</code>, <code>st.chat_message(role)</code>, <code>st.chat_input()</code> and <code>st.session_state</code> do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>st.container()</code></td><td>Group elements</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>st.chat_message(role)</code></td><td>Message bubble (user/assistant)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>st.chat_input()</code></td><td>Chat text input</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>st.session_state</code></td><td>Persist data (chat history) across reruns</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0071","card":"q-langchain-level-up-015-deploying-to-streamlit-community-cloud","sec":"langchain-level-up-s016","q":"What do you need before deploying to Streamlit Community Cloud?","a":"<p>A <strong>new public GitHub repo</strong> (separate from the course clone) with <code>app.py</code>, <code>query.py</code>, <code>docs/</code> and <code>requirements.txt</code>. <strong>Never push <code>.env</code></strong> (API keys).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0072","card":"q-langchain-level-up-015-deploying-to-streamlit-community-cloud","sec":"langchain-level-up-s016","q":"How do you create the GitHub repo for the app without pushing <code>.env</code>?","a":"<p>Add <code>.env</code>, <code>venv/</code> and <code>__pycache__/</code> to <code>.gitignore</code>, then init, commit and push.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>mkdir chat-app &amp;&amp; cd chat-app\necho &quot;.env&quot; &gt; .gitignore\necho &quot;venv/&quot; &gt;&gt; .gitignore\necho &quot;__pycache__/&quot; &gt;&gt; .gitignore\ngit init\ngit add .\ngit commit -m &quot;first commit&quot;\ngit branch -M main\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/&lt;your-username&gt;/chat-app.git\ngit push -u origin main</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0073","card":"q-langchain-level-up-015-deploying-to-streamlit-community-cloud","sec":"langchain-level-up-s016","q":"What are the steps on share.streamlit.io to deploy the app?","a":"<p>Sign in, choose <strong>Create app</strong>, pick \"Yes, I have an app\", paste the GitHub URL to <code>app.py</code> or pick repo, branch (<code>main</code>) and file. Then open <strong>Advanced settings → Secrets</strong> and Deploy. The app is served at <code>https://&lt;your-app-name&gt;.streamlit.app</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0074","card":"q-langchain-level-up-015-deploying-to-streamlit-community-cloud","sec":"langchain-level-up-s016","q":"How do you pass the OpenAI key to a deployed Streamlit app, since <code>.env</code> is not pushed?","a":"<p>Put it in Streamlit's TOML secrets and read it with <code>st.secrets</code> in code.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">TOML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>OPENAI_API_KEY = &quot;&lt;your-openai-key&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llm = ChatOpenAI(api_key=st.secrets[&quot;OPENAI_API_KEY&quot;])\nembeddings = OpenAIEmbeddings(api_key=st.secrets[&quot;OPENAI_API_KEY&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0075","card":"q-langchain-level-up-015-deploying-to-streamlit-community-cloud","sec":"langchain-level-up-s016","q":"What can you do from the Streamlit dashboard after deploying?","a":"<p>Edit with Codespaces, change the subdomain or visibility, invite collaborators, view visitor analytics and update secrets.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0076","card":"q-langchain-level-up-016-6-q-a-agent-with-multiple-data-sources-q","sec":"langchain-level-up-s017","q":"What is query analysis?","a":"<p>An intermediate step that inspects the user's question, decides <strong>which data source (retriever)</strong> to use, and produces a <strong>structured output</strong> that feeds retrieval and generation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0077","card":"q-langchain-level-up-016-6-q-a-agent-with-multiple-data-sources-q","sec":"langchain-level-up-s017","q":"What does query analysis rely on?","a":"<p><strong>Function calling</strong> (the LLM makes decisions and returns schema-conformant output) and <strong>Pydantic</strong> (defines the schema).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0078","card":"q-langchain-level-up-017-6-1-query-analyzer","sec":"langchain-level-up-s018","q":"How do you define the output schema for a query analyzer?","a":"<p>Use a Pydantic <code>BaseModel</code> with <code>Field</code> descriptions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nclass Search(BaseModel):\n    query: str = Field(description=&quot;Question asked by the user&quot;)\n    person: str = Field(description=&quot;Person targeted in the user query&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0079","card":"q-langchain-level-up-017-6-1-query-analyzer","sec":"langchain-level-up-s018","q":"How do you build a query analyzer chain with structured output?","a":"<p>Create a prompt, call <code>with_structured_output(Search)</code> on a <code>ChatOpenAI</code> model with <code>temperature=0</code>, and pipe prompt into it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llm_function_calling = ChatOpenAI(model=&quot;gpt-3.5-turbo&quot;, temperature=0)\nprompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages([\n    (&quot;system&quot;, system_message),\n    (&quot;human&quot;, &quot;{question}&quot;),\n])\nstructured_llm = llm_function_calling.with_structured_output(Search)\nquery_analyzer = prompt | structured_llm</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0080","card":"q-langchain-level-up-017-6-1-query-analyzer","sec":"langchain-level-up-s018","q":"What does the query analyzer return for \"Where did Harrison work?\"","a":"<p>A <code>Search</code> object, here <code>Search(query='work', person='HARRISON')</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>structured_output = query_analyzer.invoke({&quot;question&quot;: &quot;Where did Harrison work?&quot;})\nprint(structured_output)\n# Search(query=&#x27;work&#x27;, person=&#x27;HARRISON&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0081","card":"q-langchain-level-up-018-6-2-routing-to-a-retriever-with-a-custom","sec":"langchain-level-up-s019","q":"What is the flow of routing a query to the right retriever?","a":"<p>Query, query analysis, pick the retriever by <code>person</code>, invoke the retriever, then documents or answer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0082","card":"q-langchain-level-up-018-6-2-routing-to-a-retriever-with-a-custom","sec":"langchain-level-up-s019","q":"What does the <code>@chain</code> decorator do?","a":"<p>It turns a plain function into a Runnable.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0083","card":"q-langchain-level-up-018-6-2-routing-to-a-retriever-with-a-custom","sec":"langchain-level-up-s019","q":"How do you route a question to the retriever of the right person?","a":"<p>Keep a dict of retrievers, analyze the question, select the retriever by <code>person</code>, and invoke it with the analyzed query.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain_core.runnables import chain\n\nretrievers = {\n    &quot;HARRISON&quot;: harrison_retriever,\n    &quot;ANKUSH&quot;: ankush_retriever,\n}\n\n@chain\ndef custom_chain(question: str):\n    structured_output = query_analyzer.invoke({&quot;question&quot;: question})   # 1. analyze\n    retriever = retrievers[structured_output.person]                    # 2. select retriever\n    return retriever.invoke(structured_output.query)                    # 3. retrieve</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0084","card":"q-langchain-level-up-018-6-2-routing-to-a-retriever-with-a-custom","sec":"langchain-level-up-s019","q":"What does <code>custom_chain.invoke(\"Where did Ankush work?\")</code> return?","a":"<p>A list of documents. <code>response[0].page_content</code> is \"Ankush worked at Facebook.\"</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = custom_chain.invoke(&quot;Where did Ankush work?&quot;)\nprint(response[0].page_content)   # &quot;Ankush worked at Facebook.&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0085","card":"q-langchain-level-up-019-6-3-challenge-solution-shoes-vs-shirts-f","sec":"langchain-level-up-s020","q":"How does the shoes vs shirts schema differ from the person-based one?","a":"<p>It uses <code>category</code> instead of <code>person</code>, either 'shoes' or 'shirts'. There are two FAQ files, <code>docs/red30_shoes_faq.txt</code> and <code>docs/red30_shirts_faq.txt</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class Search(BaseModel):\n    query: str = Field(description=&quot;Query to look up&quot;)\n    category: str = Field(description=&quot;Category to use — either &#x27;shoes&#x27; or &#x27;shirts&#x27;&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0086","card":"q-langchain-level-up-019-6-3-challenge-solution-shoes-vs-shirts-f","sec":"langchain-level-up-s020","q":"How do you create one index (retriever) per FAQ file?","a":"<p>Split each file with <code>RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter</code>, create a Chroma store, take its retriever, and register both in a dict.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>text_splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=100, chunk_overlap=0)\n\ndocuments_shoes = text_splitter.split_documents(raw_text_shoes)\nvector_store_shoes = Chroma.from_documents(documents_shoes, embeddings)\nretriever_shoes = vector_store_shoes.as_retriever()\n\nretrievers = {&quot;shoes&quot;: retriever_shoes, &quot;shirts&quot;: retriever_shirts}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0087","card":"q-langchain-level-up-019-6-3-challenge-solution-shoes-vs-shirts-f","sec":"langchain-level-up-s020","q":"How does the category query analyzer take a raw string as input?","a":"<p><code>RunnablePassthrough</code> turns the raw string into <code>{\"question\": ...}</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>structured_llm = llm_function_calling.with_structured_output(Search)\nquery_analyzer = {&quot;question&quot;: RunnablePassthrough()} | prompt_query | structured_llm</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0088","card":"q-langchain-level-up-019-6-3-challenge-solution-shoes-vs-shirts-f","sec":"langchain-level-up-s020","q":"What does the category analyzer return for \"How long do we have to return shirts?\"","a":"<p><code>Search(query='return policy', category='shirts')</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>structured_output = query_analyzer.invoke(&quot;How long do we have to return shirts?&quot;)\n# Search(query=&#x27;return policy&#x27;, category=&#x27;shirts&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0089","card":"q-langchain-level-up-019-6-3-challenge-solution-shoes-vs-shirts-f","sec":"langchain-level-up-s020","q":"How does the final <code>@chain</code> route, retrieve and generate in one step?","a":"<p>It analyzes the question, picks <code>retrievers[structured_output.category]</code>, builds a RAG chain with that retriever, and invokes it with the question.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@chain\ndef query(question: str):\n    structured_output = query_analyzer.invoke(question)\n    retriever = retrievers[structured_output.category]\n    rag_chain = (\n        {&quot;context&quot;: retriever, &quot;question&quot;: RunnablePassthrough()}\n        | chat_prompt_template\n        | llm\n        | StrOutputParser()\n    )\n    return rag_chain.invoke(question)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0090","card":"q-langchain-level-up-019-6-3-challenge-solution-shoes-vs-shirts-f","sec":"langchain-level-up-s020","q":"What do the shoes and shirts questions return?","a":"<p>Returns of shirts take 30 days in original condition. The shoe types are casual, sports and business.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(query(&quot;How long do we have to return shirts?&quot;))   # 30 days, original condition\nprint(query(&quot;What type of shoes do you sell?&quot;))         # casual, sports, business</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0091","card":"q-langchain-level-up-019-6-3-challenge-solution-shoes-vs-shirts-f","sec":"langchain-level-up-s020","q":"What is the execution flow of the shoes vs shirts agent?","a":"<p>User query, <code>query_analyzer</code> (<code>category</code>), <code>retrievers[category]</code>, RAG chain (context, prompt, LLM, parser), answer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0092","card":"q-langchain-level-up-020-7-semantic-search-with-mongodb-atlas-vec","sec":"langchain-level-up-s021","q":"What is MongoDB Atlas Vector Search?","a":"<p>A feature that finds related objects by <strong>semantic similarity</strong> using embeddings from providers such as OpenAI, AWS and Google. It integrates with LangChain for RAG.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0093","card":"q-langchain-level-up-020-7-semantic-search-with-mongodb-atlas-vec","sec":"langchain-level-up-s021","q":"Which query types does Atlas Vector Search support?","a":"<p><strong>Semantic search</strong> (vector similarity) and <strong>hybrid search</strong> (semantic plus full-text).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0094","card":"q-langchain-level-up-021-7-1-atlas-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s022","q":"How do you set up the Atlas cluster, database and collection for the course?","a":"<p>Sign up at mongodb.com/atlas and deploy a <strong>Free (512 MB)</strong> cluster (for example <code>ClusterLangChain</code>, any of AWS/GCP/Azure, nearest region). Under Browse Collections create the database <code>elearning</code> with the collection <code>mongodb-training</code>. Then Connect, Drivers, Python and copy the connection string.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0095","card":"q-langchain-level-up-021-7-1-atlas-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s022","q":"Which database user and role do you need for Atlas Vector Search, and why?","a":"<p>Under <strong>Security → Database Access</strong>, a user with password auth and the <strong>Atlas Admin</strong> built-in role. The role is required to create the vector search index. Without valid credentials the connection fails with an authentication error.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0096","card":"q-langchain-level-up-021-7-1-atlas-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s022","q":"Which values go into the <code>.env</code> file for the Atlas project?","a":"<p>The Atlas connection string, the OpenAI key, the database name, the collection name and the vector index name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># .env\nATLAS_CONNECTION_STRING=&quot;mongodb+srv://&lt;username&gt;:&lt;password&gt;@clusterlangchain.xxxxx.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&amp;w=majority&quot;\nOPENAI_API_KEY=&quot;&lt;your-openai-api-key&gt;&quot;\nDB_NAME=&quot;elearning&quot;\nCOLLECTION_NAME=&quot;mongodb-training&quot;\nVECTOR_SEARCH_INDEX=&quot;vector_index&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0097","card":"q-langchain-level-up-021-7-1-atlas-setup","sec":"langchain-level-up-s022","q":"How do you connect to the Atlas cluster from Python and check the connection?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>client = MongoClient(ATLAS_CONNECTION_STRING)\ncollection = client[DB_NAME][COLLECTION_NAME]\n\nif client:\n    print(&quot;Successfully connected to MongoDB Atlas&quot;)\n    print(client.list_database_names())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0098","card":"q-langchain-level-up-022-7-2-load-data-and-create-the-vector-stor","sec":"langchain-level-up-s023","q":"What is the pipeline that loads the PDF into the Atlas vector store?","a":"<p>PDF (MongoDB Atlas best practices), <code>PyPDFLoader</code>, <code>RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter</code> (200 chars, 20 overlap), then <code>MongoDBAtlasVectorSearch.from_documents</code>. It embeds with OpenAI, stores in the collection and references the search index.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0099","card":"q-langchain-level-up-022-7-2-load-data-and-create-the-vector-stor","sec":"langchain-level-up-s023","q":"How do you load and split the PDF for Atlas?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>loader = PyPDFLoader(&quot;https://query.prod.cms.rt.microsoft.com/cms/api/am/binary/RE4HkJP&quot;)\ndata = loader.load()\n\ntext_splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=200, chunk_overlap=20)\ndocuments = text_splitter.split_documents(data)\nprint(documents[0])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0100","card":"q-langchain-level-up-022-7-2-load-data-and-create-the-vector-stor","sec":"langchain-level-up-s023","q":"How do you create the Atlas vector store, and what must <code>index_name</code> match?","a":"<p>Call <code>MongoDBAtlasVectorSearch.from_documents</code> with the documents, embeddings, collection and <code>index_name</code>. The index name must match the Atlas index name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>embeddings = OpenAIEmbeddings()\nvector_store = MongoDBAtlasVectorSearch.from_documents(\n    documents,\n    embeddings,\n    collection=collection,\n    index_name=VECTOR_SEARCH_INDEX,   # must match the Atlas index name\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0101","card":"q-langchain-level-up-023-7-3-create-the-atlas-vector-search-index","sec":"langchain-level-up-s024","q":"How do you create the Atlas Vector Search index in the UI?","a":"<p>Go to Database, your cluster, <strong>Atlas Search</strong>, <strong>Atlas Vector Search</strong>, <strong>JSON Editor</strong>. Pick <code>elearning</code> / <code>mongodb-training</code> and the index name <code>vector_index</code>, paste the definition, and Create. Wait for <strong>Active</strong>. It requires Atlas Admin, and the <code>index_name</code> in Python must match exactly.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0102","card":"q-langchain-level-up-023-7-3-create-the-atlas-vector-search-index","sec":"langchain-level-up-s024","q":"What does the vector index definition look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{\n  &quot;fields&quot;: [\n    {\n      &quot;type&quot;: &quot;vector&quot;,\n      &quot;path&quot;: &quot;embedding&quot;,\n      &quot;numDimensions&quot;: 1536,\n      &quot;similarity&quot;: &quot;cosine&quot;\n    }\n  ]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0103","card":"q-langchain-level-up-023-7-3-create-the-atlas-vector-search-index","sec":"langchain-level-up-s024","q":"What do <code>path</code>, <code>numDimensions</code> and <code>similarity</code> mean in the Atlas vector index?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>path</code></td><td>Document field holding the vector embedding</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>numDimensions</code></td><td>1536 = OpenAI <code>text-embedding-ada-002</code> output size</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>similarity</code></td><td>Metric: <code>cosine</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0104","card":"q-langchain-level-up-023-7-3-create-the-atlas-vector-search-index","sec":"langchain-level-up-s024","q":"What happens if the vector index does not exist yet, and what does running <code>query.py</code> load?","a":"<p>Vector store initialization fails until the index exists. Running <code>query.py</code> loads 20 chunk documents (text plus embedding) into the collection.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0105","card":"q-langchain-level-up-024-7-4-similarity-search","sec":"langchain-level-up-s025","q":"What is the role of <code>query.py</code> and <code>main.py</code> in the Atlas semantic search project?","a":"<p><code>query.py</code> loads data, creates the store and runs searches. <code>main.py</code> is a terminal UI.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0106","card":"q-langchain-level-up-024-7-4-similarity-search","sec":"langchain-level-up-s025","q":"How do you run a similarity search on Atlas and get the best chunk text?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def query_data(query: str):\n    results = vector_store.similarity_search(query)\n    return results[0].page_content\n\nprint(query_data(&quot;MongoDB deployment&quot;))\nprint(query_data(&quot;MongoDB security&quot;))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0107","card":"q-langchain-level-up-025-7-5-retrieval-rag-chain","sec":"langchain-level-up-s026","q":"What does the Atlas RAG prompt contain, and what does it tell the model about unknown answers?","a":"<p>Two placeholders, <code>{context}</code> (docs from Atlas) and <code>{question}</code>. It tells the model to say it doesn't know instead of inventing an answer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>template = &quot;&quot;&quot;Use the following pieces of context to answer the question at the end.\nIf you don&#x27;t know the answer, just say that you don&#x27;t know. Don&#x27;t try to make up an answer.\n{context}\nQuestion: {question}\n&quot;&quot;&quot;\ncustom_rag_prompt = PromptTemplate.from_template(template)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0108","card":"q-langchain-level-up-025-7-5-retrieval-rag-chain","sec":"langchain-level-up-s026","q":"How do you configure the Atlas retriever to return only the best document?","a":"<p>Use <code>as_retriever</code> with <code>search_type=\"similarity\"</code> (cosine) and <code>search_kwargs={\"k\": 1}</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retriever = vector_store.as_retriever(\n    search_type=&quot;similarity&quot;,\n    search_kwargs={&quot;k&quot;: 1},\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0109","card":"q-langchain-level-up-025-7-5-retrieval-rag-chain","sec":"langchain-level-up-s026","q":"How do you build the Atlas RAG chain, and why add <code>StrOutputParser()</code>?","a":"<p>Pipe the context/question dict into the prompt, the LLM and the parser. Without a parser the result is a raw <code>AIMessage</code>. With <code>StrOutputParser()</code> it is a string.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llm = ChatOpenAI(model=&quot;gpt-3.5-turbo&quot;, temperature=0)\nrag_chain = (\n    {&quot;context&quot;: retriever, &quot;question&quot;: RunnablePassthrough()}\n    | custom_rag_prompt\n    | llm\n    | StrOutputParser()\n)\nanswer = rag_chain.invoke(&quot;How can I secure my MongoDB Atlas cluster?&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0110","card":"q-langchain-level-up-025-7-5-retrieval-rag-chain","sec":"langchain-level-up-s026","q":"How do you wrap the Atlas RAG chain in a function for <code>main.py</code>?","a":"<p>Invoke the chain, print the answer in blue and return it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def query_data(query: str):\n    answer = rag_chain.invoke(query)\n    print(f&quot;\\033[94m{answer}\\033[0m&quot;)  # print in blue\n    return answer</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0111","card":"q-langchain-level-up-025-7-5-retrieval-rag-chain","sec":"langchain-level-up-s026","q":"What happens when you ask the Atlas RAG chatbot something outside the PDF?","a":"<p>It returns an \"I don't have enough information\" answer, because the prompt instruction prevents hallucination. An example is \"How to create a vector store?\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0112","card":"q-langchain-level-up-026-8-agents-tools-over-mongodb-openai-tools","sec":"langchain-level-up-s027","q":"What is an agent in the Level Up course, and which two tools does it use?","a":"<p>An agent uses an LLM with function calling to choose among <strong>tools</strong> (Python functions) and call them. Tool 1 is MongoDB Atlas vector search over PDF docs. Tool 2 is web search over an HTML page (<code>WebBaseLoader</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0113","card":"q-langchain-level-up-026-8-agents-tools-over-mongodb-openai-tools","sec":"langchain-level-up-s027","q":"How does the agent choose a tool, and what can it do when the vector index lacks the answer?","a":"<p>It picks the tool from the query and the tool descriptions. It can fall back to the web when the vector index lacks the answer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0114","card":"q-langchain-level-up-027-8-1-defining-tools","sec":"langchain-level-up-s028","q":"How do you define a tool in LangChain, and what are its name, description and arguments?","a":"<p>Decorate a function with <code>@tool</code>. The name is the function name, the description is the <strong>docstring</strong>, and the arguments are the typed parameters.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain_core.tools import tool\n\n@tool\ndef get_word_length(word: str) -&gt; int:\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;Returns the length of a word.&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    return len(word)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0115","card":"q-langchain-level-up-027-8-1-defining-tools","sec":"langchain-level-up-s028","q":"Why is the docstring mandatory in a LangChain <code>@tool</code> function?","a":"<p>The LLM reads it to decide when and how to use the tool, and validation fails without it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0116","card":"q-langchain-level-up-027-8-1-defining-tools","sec":"langchain-level-up-s028","q":"How do you wrap the Atlas RAG chain as a tool?","a":"<p>Import the chain from <code>vector_search_index.py</code> and call it inside a <code>@tool</code> function with a docstring.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from retrievers.vector_search_index import rag_chain\n\n@tool\ndef vector_search_query(query: str) -&gt; str:\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;Queries the MongoDB Atlas vector search index to retrieve\n    relevant documents and generate an answer.&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    response = rag_chain.invoke(query)\n    return response</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0117","card":"q-langchain-level-up-028-8-2-agent-prompt-bind-tools-build-the-ag","sec":"langchain-level-up-s029","q":"What are <code>input</code> and <code>agent_scratchpad</code> in the agent prompt?","a":"<p><code>input</code> is the user query. <code>agent_scratchpad</code> holds intermediate tool calls and results, which enable multi-step reasoning.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages([\n    (&quot;system&quot;, &quot;You are a helpful assistant.&quot;),\n    (&quot;human&quot;, &quot;{input}&quot;),\n    MessagesPlaceholder(variable_name=&quot;agent_scratchpad&quot;),\n])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0118","card":"q-langchain-level-up-028-8-2-agent-prompt-bind-tools-build-the-ag","sec":"langchain-level-up-s029","q":"How do you attach tools to the LLM?","a":"<p>Call <code>bind_tools</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tools = [get_word_length, vector_search_query]\nllm_with_tools = llm.bind_tools(tools)    # attach tool definitions to the LLM</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0119","card":"q-langchain-level-up-028-8-2-agent-prompt-bind-tools-build-the-ag","sec":"langchain-level-up-s029","q":"How do you assemble the OpenAI tools agent chain?","a":"<p>Map <code>input</code> and the formatted <code>agent_scratchpad</code>, then pipe into the prompt, the LLM with tools and <code>OpenAIToolsAgentOutputParser()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain.agents.format_scratchpad.openai_tools import format_to_openai_tool_messages\nfrom langchain.agents.output_parsers.openai_tools import OpenAIToolsAgentOutputParser\n\nagent = (\n    {\n        &quot;input&quot;: lambda x: x[&quot;input&quot;],\n        &quot;agent_scratchpad&quot;: lambda x: format_to_openai_tool_messages(x[&quot;intermediate_steps&quot;]),\n    }\n    | prompt\n    | llm_with_tools\n    | OpenAIToolsAgentOutputParser()\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0120","card":"q-langchain-level-up-028-8-2-agent-prompt-bind-tools-build-the-ag","sec":"langchain-level-up-s029","q":"What do <code>bind_tools()</code>, <code>format_to_openai_tool_messages</code> and <code>OpenAIToolsAgentOutputParser</code> do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>bind_tools()</code></td><td>Attaches tool definitions to the LLM</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>format_to_openai_tool_messages</code></td><td>Converts intermediate steps into scratchpad messages</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>OpenAIToolsAgentOutputParser</code></td><td>Parses LLM output into an <code>AgentAction</code> (call tool) or <code>AgentFinish</code> (final answer)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0121","card":"q-langchain-level-up-029-8-3-agentexecutor","sec":"langchain-level-up-s030","q":"What does <code>AgentExecutor</code> do?","a":"<p>It runs the loop: the agent decides, calls a tool, feeds the result back, and gives a final answer. <code>verbose=True</code> prints the trace.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0122","card":"q-langchain-level-up-029-8-3-agentexecutor","sec":"langchain-level-up-s030","q":"How do you create and run an <code>AgentExecutor</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from langchain.agents import AgentExecutor\n\nagent_executor = AgentExecutor(agent=agent, tools=tools, verbose=True)\n\ndef run_agent(query: str):\n    response = agent_executor.invoke({&quot;input&quot;: query})\n    print(response[&quot;output&quot;])\n\nrun_agent(&quot;How to secure a MongoDB Atlas cluster?&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0123","card":"q-langchain-level-up-029-8-3-agentexecutor","sec":"langchain-level-up-s030","q":"What does <code>AgentExecutor.invoke</code> return?","a":"<p>A dict <code>{\"input\": ..., \"output\": ...}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0124","card":"q-langchain-level-up-030-8-4-multitask-agent-challenge-solution","sec":"langchain-level-up-s031","q":"What problem does the multitask agent solve and what is the fix?","a":"<p>\"How to create a vector store?\" returns \"I don't know\" because the PDF covers best practices, not tutorials. The fix is to add a second tool backed by an HTML page and tighten the system prompt.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0125","card":"q-langchain-level-up-030-8-4-multitask-agent-challenge-solution","sec":"langchain-level-up-s031","q":"What system prompt does the multitask agent use?","a":"<p>It says the assistant is powerful but doesn't know current events, should say 'I don't know' if unsure, and must not make up an answer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages([\n    (&quot;system&quot;,\n     &quot;You are a very powerful assistant, but don&#x27;t know current events.\\n&quot;\n     &quot;If you don&#x27;t know the answer, just say &#x27;I don&#x27;t know&#x27;.\\n&quot;\n     &quot;Do not try to make up an answer.&quot;),\n    (&quot;human&quot;, &quot;{input}&quot;),\n    MessagesPlaceholder(variable_name=&quot;agent_scratchpad&quot;),\n])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0126","card":"q-langchain-level-up-030-8-4-multitask-agent-challenge-solution","sec":"langchain-level-up-s031","q":"How do you build the web search retriever of the second tool?","a":"<p>Load the page with <code>WebBaseLoader</code>, split it, store it in Chroma and take the retriever.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>loader = WebBaseLoader(&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-vector-search/vector-search-overview/&quot;)\ndata = loader.load()\ntext_splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=200, chunk_overlap=20)\ndocuments = text_splitter.split_documents(data)\nvector_store = Chroma.from_documents(documents, OpenAIEmbeddings())\nretriever = vector_store.as_retriever()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0127","card":"q-langchain-level-up-030-8-4-multitask-agent-challenge-solution","sec":"langchain-level-up-s031","q":"How does the web search chain get its prompt?","a":"<p>It pulls the pre-built prompt <code>rlm/rag-prompt</code> from LangChain Hub.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt = hub.pull(&quot;rlm/rag-prompt&quot;)     # pre-built prompt from LangChain Hub\nllm = ChatOpenAI(model=&quot;gpt-3.5-turbo&quot;, temperature=0)\n\nweb_search_chain = (\n    {&quot;context&quot;: retriever, &quot;question&quot;: RunnablePassthrough()}\n    | prompt\n    | llm\n    | StrOutputParser()\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0128","card":"q-langchain-level-up-030-8-4-multitask-agent-challenge-solution","sec":"langchain-level-up-s031","q":"How do you add the web search tool to the agent?","a":"<p>Wrap <code>web_search_chain</code> in a <code>@tool</code> function, add it to <code>tools</code> and bind the tools again.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@tool\ndef web_search_query(query: str) -&gt; str:\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;Search queries using web search for additional information.&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    response = web_search_chain.invoke(query)\n    return response\n\ntools = [vector_search_query, web_search_query]\nllm_with_tools = llm.bind_tools(tools)\nagent_executor = AgentExecutor(agent=agent, tools=tools, verbose=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0129","card":"q-langchain-level-up-030-8-4-multitask-agent-challenge-solution","sec":"langchain-level-up-s031","q":"Which tool does the agent pick for \"How to create a vector store?\" and \"What is vector search?\"","a":"<p><code>web_search_query</code> for both.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>run_agent(&quot;How to create a vector store?&quot;)   # agent picks web_search_query\nrun_agent(&quot;What is vector search?&quot;)          # agent picks web_search_query</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0130","card":"q-langchain-level-up-030-8-4-multitask-agent-challenge-solution","sec":"langchain-level-up-s031","q":"<code>vector_search_query</code> vs <code>web_search_query</code>: which data and best for what?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Data source</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>vector_search_query</code></td><td>Atlas (PDF)</td><td>Best practices, security, deployment</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>web_search_query</code></td><td>Web (HTML page)</td><td>Tutorials, how-to, vector search overview</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0131","card":"q-langchain-level-up-030-8-4-multitask-agent-challenge-solution","sec":"langchain-level-up-s031","q":"How does the agent choose between tools, and what follows from that?","a":"<p>It chooses only from tool names and docstrings, so write clear docstrings.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0132","card":"q-langchain-level-up-031-10-deploying-chains-as-a-rest-api-with-l","sec":"langchain-level-up-s033","q":"What is LangServe?","a":"<p>A tool that deploys <strong>runnables and chains as a REST API</strong>. It builds on FastAPI (server) and Pydantic (validation) and auto-generates JSON Schema and Swagger docs, so endpoints can be tested in the browser.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0133","card":"q-langchain-level-up-031-10-deploying-chains-as-a-rest-api-with-l","sec":"langchain-level-up-s033","q":"How do you install LangServe, and what does <code>uvicorn</code> do?","a":"<p><code>pip install langserve[all] fastapi uvicorn</code>. <code>uvicorn</code> is the ASGI server that runs the FastAPI app.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install langserve[all] fastapi uvicorn</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0134","card":"q-langchain-level-up-031-10-deploying-chains-as-a-rest-api-with-l","sec":"langchain-level-up-s033","q":"What files does the LangServe project have?","a":"<p><code>server.py</code> (FastAPI plus routes), <code>.env</code>, <code>requirements.txt</code> and a README.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0135","card":"q-langchain-level-up-032-10-1-server-routes-run","sec":"langchain-level-up-s034","q":"What is the workflow to deploy a chain with LangServe?","a":"<p>Create a FastAPI server, create runnables, <code>add_routes</code>, run with Uvicorn, and open Swagger UI at <code>/docs</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0136","card":"q-langchain-level-up-032-10-1-server-routes-run","sec":"langchain-level-up-s034","q":"How do you create the FastAPI app of the LangServe server?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app = FastAPI(\n    title=&quot;LangChain Server&quot;,\n    version=&quot;1.0&quot;,\n    description=&quot;A simple API server using LangChain&#x27;s Runnable interfaces&quot;,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0137","card":"q-langchain-level-up-032-10-1-server-routes-run","sec":"langchain-level-up-s034","q":"How do you build a joke chain with a custom parser for LangServe?","a":"<p>Pipe a prompt and model into a <code>RunnableLambda</code> that returns <code>response.content</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model = ChatOpenAI(model=&quot;gpt-3.5-turbo&quot;, temperature=0)\nprompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(&quot;Tell me a joke about {topic}&quot;)\n\n# Parse the AIMessage into a string\ndef parsed_response(response):\n    return response.content\n\nchain = prompt | model | RunnableLambda(parsed_response)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0138","card":"q-langchain-level-up-032-10-1-server-routes-run","sec":"langchain-level-up-s034","q":"How do you add routes and run the LangServe server from Python?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>add_routes(app, model, path=&quot;/openai&quot;)\nadd_routes(app, chain, path=&quot;/joke&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    import uvicorn\n    uvicorn.run(app, host=&quot;localhost&quot;, port=8000)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0139","card":"q-langchain-level-up-032-10-1-server-routes-run","sec":"langchain-level-up-s034","q":"Which endpoints does each <code>add_routes(app, runnable, path=...)</code> call create?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>Method</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>&lt;path&gt;/invoke</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Single input</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>&lt;path&gt;/batch</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Multiple inputs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>&lt;path&gt;/stream</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Stream output</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>&lt;path&gt;/stream_log</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Stream with logging</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>&lt;path&gt;/docs</code></td><td>GET</td><td>Swagger UI for the route</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>/docs</code></td><td>GET</td><td>Global Swagger UI</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0140","card":"q-langchain-level-up-032-10-1-server-routes-run","sec":"langchain-level-up-s034","q":"How do you run the server with the Uvicorn command line, and what does <code>--reload</code> do?","a":"<p><code>--reload</code> auto-restarts on file changes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>uvicorn server:app --host localhost --port 8000\nuvicorn server:app --reload     # auto-restart on file changes</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0141","card":"q-langchain-level-up-032-10-1-server-routes-run","sec":"langchain-level-up-s034","q":"What do you do if the invoke, batch and stream schemas do not show in Swagger?","a":"<p>Downgrade Pydantic.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install &quot;pydantic&lt;2.8.2&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0142","card":"q-langchain-level-up-032-10-1-server-routes-run","sec":"langchain-level-up-s034","q":"How do you test a LangServe route with cURL, and what shape does the body have?","a":"<p>The body is <code>{\"input\": ...}</code>. For a prompt chain, <code>input</code> is a dict of template variables.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/joke/invoke \\\n  -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; \\\n  -d &#x27;{&quot;input&quot;: {&quot;topic&quot;: &quot;cats&quot;}}&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0143","card":"q-langchain-level-up-033-10-2-challenge-solution-serve-the-atlas","sec":"langchain-level-up-s035","q":"How do you serve the Atlas RAG chain through LangServe?","a":"<p>Reuse the retrieval chain from the Atlas section and add a third route to <code>server.py</code>. The <code>.env</code> needs <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code>, <code>ATLAS_CONNECTION_STRING</code>, <code>DB_NAME</code>, <code>COLLECTION_NAME</code> and <code>VECTOR_SEARCH_INDEX</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from retrievers.vector_search_index import retrieval_chain\n\nadd_routes(app, retrieval_chain, path=&quot;/query&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0144","card":"q-langchain-level-up-033-10-2-challenge-solution-serve-the-atlas","sec":"langchain-level-up-s035","q":"Which routes does the final <code>server.py</code> expose?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Runnable</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>/openai</code></td><td><code>ChatOpenAI</code> model</td><td>Direct LLM</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>/joke</code></td><td><code>prompt | model | RunnableLambda</code></td><td>Joke chain</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>/query</code></td><td><code>retrieval_chain</code></td><td>RAG over Atlas Vector Search (PDF)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0145","card":"q-langchain-level-up-033-10-2-challenge-solution-serve-the-atlas","sec":"langchain-level-up-s035","q":"How do you call the <code>/query/invoke</code> route from a Python client?","a":"<p>Post <code>{\"input\": ...}</code> and read <code>response.json()[\"output\"]</code>. You can also test it in Swagger at <code>/query/invoke</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import requests\nresponse = requests.post(\n    &quot;http://localhost:8000/query/invoke&quot;,\n    json={&quot;input&quot;: &quot;How to secure a database?&quot;}\n)\nprint(response.json()[&quot;output&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0146","card":"q-langchain-level-up-034-11-deploying-to-the-cloud-with-render","sec":"langchain-level-up-s036","q":"What is Render and what does deploying there require?","a":"<p>A cloud app hosting platform with a free tier. It requires a <strong>personal GitHub account</strong> and a <strong>separate repository</strong>. The cloned exercise repo cannot be used. Sign up with GitHub so Render pulls straight from your repo.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0147","card":"q-langchain-level-up-034-11-deploying-to-the-cloud-with-render","sec":"langchain-level-up-s036","q":"Which files should the <code>.gitignore</code> of the Render project contain?","a":"<p>Never push secrets, so ignore these:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>.env\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n.venv/</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0148","card":"q-langchain-level-up-034-11-deploying-to-the-cloud-with-render","sec":"langchain-level-up-s036","q":"How do you push the LangServe project to GitHub for Render?","a":"<p>Create a public repo <code>rag-rest-web-service</code> on GitHub first (README and .gitignore unchecked), then init, commit and push.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>git init\ngit add .\ngit commit -m &quot;first commit&quot;\ngit branch -M main\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/&lt;username&gt;/rag-rest-web-service.git\ngit push -u origin main</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0149","card":"q-langchain-level-up-034-11-deploying-to-the-cloud-with-render","sec":"langchain-level-up-s036","q":"How do you create the Render web service and which settings do you use?","a":"<p>Dashboard, New, <strong>Web Service</strong>, build and deploy from a Git repository, then connect the repo.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Name</td><td><code>rag-rest-web-service</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Start Command</td><td><code>uvicorn server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Plan</td><td>Free</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0150","card":"q-langchain-level-up-034-11-deploying-to-the-cloud-with-render","sec":"langchain-level-up-s036","q":"How do you give a Render deployment its secrets, since <code>.env</code> is not in GitHub?","a":"<p>Set environment variables in Render: <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code>, <code>ATLAS_CONNECTION_STRING</code> (if using MongoDB), <code>DB_NAME</code> and <code>COLLECTION_NAME</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0151","card":"q-langchain-level-up-034-11-deploying-to-the-cloud-with-render","sec":"langchain-level-up-s036","q":"How do you check that the Render deployment works?","a":"<p>Deploy, wait for status <strong>Live</strong>, then test <code>https://rag-rest-web-service.onrender.com/docs</code> (for example <code>/joke/invoke</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0152","card":"q-langchain-level-up-034-11-deploying-to-the-cloud-with-render","sec":"langchain-level-up-s036","q":"Why does the Render start command use <code>--host 0.0.0.0</code> and not <code>localhost</code>?","a":"<p><code>0.0.0.0</code> is needed in a hosted container, while <code>localhost</code> is for local runs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0153","card":"q-langchain-level-up-035-12-course-recap-core-components","sec":"langchain-level-up-s037","q":"What are the course chapters and their key skills?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Chapter</th><th>Topic</th><th>Key skills</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>2</td><td>LangChain basics</td><td>Chains, prompt templates, output parsers, LCEL</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>3</td><td>Similarity search &amp; context</td><td>FAISS, embeddings, vector stores, retrievers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>4</td><td>LLMs with RAG</td><td>Loading/splitting, Chroma, chat history</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>5</td><td>Streamlit app</td><td>Layout, functionality, Streamlit Cloud deploy</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>6</td><td>Multiple data inputs</td><td>Query analysis, Pydantic, function calling, retriever routing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>7</td><td>MongoDB Atlas Vector Search</td><td>Cluster, vector index, semantic search, RAG chain</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>8</td><td>NoSQL/agents</td><td><code>@tool</code>, multitask agents, <code>AgentExecutor</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>10</td><td>LangServe</td><td>FastAPI, routes, Swagger UI</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>11</td><td>Cloud deploy</td><td>GitHub, Render</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0154","card":"q-langchain-level-up-035-12-course-recap-core-components","sec":"langchain-level-up-s037","q":"What is the purpose of the core LangChain components <code>ChatOpenAI</code>, <code>ChatPromptTemplate</code>, <code>RunnablePassthrough</code>, <code>StrOutputParser</code> and <code>RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>ChatOpenAI</code></td><td>LLM interface</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>ChatPromptTemplate</code></td><td>Structured prompts</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>RunnablePassthrough</code></td><td>Pass data through chains</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>StrOutputParser</code></td><td>LLM output → string</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter</code></td><td>Chunk documents</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0155","card":"q-langchain-level-up-035-12-course-recap-core-components","sec":"langchain-level-up-s037","q":"Which vector stores, agent tools and deploy helper does the recap list?","a":"<p><code>Chroma</code> / <code>FAISS</code> / <code>MongoDBAtlasVectorSearch</code> are vector stores. <code>@tool</code> + <code>AgentExecutor</code> handle agent tool usage. <code>add_routes</code> (LangServe) deploys chains as REST APIs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"langchain-level-up-f0156","card":"q-langchain-level-up-035-12-course-recap-core-components","sec":"langchain-level-up-s037","q":"What next steps does the course suggest?","a":"<p>Advanced agent patterns and multi-agent architectures, plus production RAG with evaluation and monitoring.</p>","hand":true}];
